 { With a bishop's pawn on the seventh rank, White's only matter of concern is a mating net. } 1. { -KEY- } Kb8 $4 { A natural, but losing move. } ( 1. Ka8 $1 { saved a draw - Baburin. Let's make a few more moves: } Kc5 2. c8=Q Kb6 3. Qb8 $1 Ka6 4. Qc8 { and White repels the attack, thanks to the additional square on b8 freed by the king move to a8. By the way, } 4. Qd6 $5 { exploiting the stalemate motif works as well. } ) 
Kc5 2. c8=Q+ ( { The game actually went } 2. Ka8 Qd7 3. Kb8 Kb6 { and White resigned, in view of } 4. c8=Q $11 Qa7 ) 
Kb6 { Despite the material balance and reduced number of pieces, mate is inevitable. } 
 *

