[Black "Example 309- Hellsten- J. vs. Lindgren- F.- Sollentuna 1995"]
[Result "*"]
[FEN "6k1/p1q2p2/2P3pp/1Q6/3p3P/8/5PP1/6K1 b - - 0 1"]

 { The fact that Black has an extra pawn isn't too relevant here - as often occurs in queen endings, what really counts is who has the more advanced passed pawn. Anyway, his salvation was just around the corner. } 1... { -KEY- } Qf4 $1 { Preparing a perpetual. } ( { a) Instead, the game went } 1... d3 $2 2. Qb7 Qf4 $2 ( { losing at once, although after } 2... d2 3. Qxc7 d1=Q 4. Kh2 { White should also win } ) 
3. c7 Qc1 4. Kh2 Qf4 5. g3 Qxf2 6. Qg2 Qf5 7. Qa8 Kh7 8. c8=Q $11 { and Black soon resigned. } ) 
 ( { b) Incidentally, } 1... Kf8 $2 2. Qb7 { is just as bad. } ) 
2. Qb7 ( { a) There is nothing better; e.g. } 2. Qc5 Qc7 $1 3. Qd5 Kf8 ) 
 ( { b) Or } 2. g3 Qc1 3. Kg2 d3 ) 
 ( { c) While } 2. Qd5 { permits } d3 $1 { intending } 3. Qxd3 Qc1 ) 
Qc1+ 3. Kh2 Qf4+ 4. Kh3 Qf5+ 5. Kg3 Qe5+ ( { White can't escape the checks; e.g. } 5... Qe5 6. Kf3 Qd5 7. Ke2 Qc4 ) 

