[Result "*"]
[FEN "8/8/6kp/Pq3p2/8/5QPK/7P/8 w - - 0 1"]

 { White's unsafe king makes it difficult to profit on the passed pawn, a fact that led Brynell into a fatal decision. } 1. { -KEY- } Qc3 $4 { Saving the pawn, but abandoning the king! } ( { a) Actually, the queen is unable to protect both of them in this position; e.g. } 1. Qa3 Qf1 2. Kh4 Qc4 ( { not } 2. Qc3 Qg2 $2 3. Qd6 ) 
3. Kh3 Qf1 { with a perpetual. } ) 
 ( { b) Or } 1. Qa8 Kh5 $1 ( { the slower } 1. Qc3 Qf1 2. Qg2 Qc4 3. Qd2 Qf1 4. Kh4 Qc4 5. Qf4 Qa6 { should also work; } ) 
2. a6 Qe2 { and a perpetual along g4-e2 again saves Black. } ) 
Qf1+ { Starting to weave a mating net. } ( { The game, haunted by mutual time-trouble at this point, instead saw } 1... Kh5 $4 2. Qe1 { and White went on to win. } ) 
2. Kh4 Qg2 $1 { The right square, in order to threaten mate and prevent the check on c6 at the same time. } 3. h3 Qe4+ 4. g4 f4 $1 ( { The mate is inevitable; e.g. } 4... f4 5. Qc5 ( { or } 4... f4 4. Qb2 Qe7 ) 
Qe1 { - Brynell. } ) 

 *

